+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are only shown when `-l/--links`
+is in use; without it they are skipped and a notice is logged. With
+`-l/--links` a link is listed under its name plus a `.rclonelink`
+suffix, its size is the length of the target, and reading it returns
+the target path. This is the same convention the other backends, such
+as [local](/local/#symlinks--junction-points), use.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+```
+
+Copying with `-l/--links` recreates the link on a destination which
+supports them:
+
+```
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
